---
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Mermaid from '../components/Mermaid.astro';
import { withBase } from '../utils/url';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead
			title="Learning paths"
			description="Suggested routes through Linux internals — from boot to memory, syscalls, and reading kernel source."
		/>
	</head>
	<body>
		<Header />
		<main>
			<header class="page-head animate-rise">
				<h1>Learning paths</h1>
				<p>
					Pick a trail. Each path points at notes on this site and classic open sources (kernel
					docs, LWN, man pages) so you can learn without paying for a course.
				</p>
			</header>

			<section class="path animate-rise-delay">
				<h2>Path A — From power-on to PID 1</h2>
				<p>Follow the machine from firmware into the kernel and the first userspace process.</p>
				<pre class="mermaid">
flowchart TD
  A[Firmware / UEFI] --> B[Bootloader]
  B --> C[Kernel decompress + setup]
  C --> D[start_kernel]
  D --> E[init / systemd]
  E --> F[Userspace]
				</pre>
				<ul>
					<li><a href={withBase('blog/how-the-kernel-boots')}>How the kernel boots</a></li>
					<li>
						External: <a href="https://docs.kernel.org/admin-guide/init.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
							>kernel.org — init</a
						>
					</li>
				</ul>
			</section>

			<section class="path">
				<h2>Path B — Process &amp; scheduler</h2>
				<p>What is a task_struct, how does fork work, and who runs next?</p>
				<pre class="mermaid">
flowchart LR
  fork[fork / clone] --> ts[task_struct]
  ts --> rq[runqueue]
  rq --> pick[pick_next_task]
  pick --> switch[context_switch]
				</pre>
				<ul>
					<li><a href={withBase('blog/anatomy-of-a-linux-process')}>Anatomy of a Linux process</a></li>
					<li>
						External: <a href="https://docs.kernel.org/scheduler/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
							>kernel.org — scheduler</a
						>
					</li>
				</ul>
			</section>

			<section class="path">
				<h2>Path C — Memory &amp; syscalls</h2>
				<p>Cross the userspace/kernel boundary, then walk virtual memory.</p>
				<pre class="mermaid">
sequenceDiagram
  participant App
  participant libc
  participant Kernel
  App->>libc: open(...)
  libc->>Kernel: syscall
  Kernel-->>libc: fd / errno
  libc-->>App: return
				</pre>
				<ul>
					<li><a href={withBase('blog/syscalls-crossing-the-boundary')}>Syscalls: crossing the boundary</a></li>
					<li><a href={withBase('blog/virtual-memory-walkthrough')}>Virtual memory walkthrough</a></li>
					<li><a href={withBase('blog/reading-kernel-source')}>Reading kernel source: where to start</a></li>
				</ul>
			</section>
		</main>
		<Footer />
		<Mermaid />
	</body>
</html>

<style>
	main {
		width: var(--max);
		max-width: calc(100% - 2em);
	}
	.page-head p {
		color: var(--ink-muted);
	}
	.path {
		margin: 2.5rem 0;
		padding: 1.5rem;
		background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8);
		border: 1px solid var(--line);
		border-radius: var(--radius);
	}
	.path h2 {
		margin-top: 0;
	}
	.path p {
		color: var(--ink-muted);
	}
</style>
